prs.body:
Closes the remaining source-side control-plane evidence bridge for merged #538 without weakening the founder-private vault boundary.

Adds `src/founder-ops-runtime-probe.mjs`:
- derives a canonical non-secret runtime identity from platform/environment/region/exact source commit;
- accepts only an observed HTTP 200 `FOUNDER_OPS_READ_ONLY` view bound to the expected exact source commit;
- requires the live view to report raw Personal Civilization unreachable, private vault data excluded, network life-state access unauthorized, and businessEffectAuthority NONE;
- requires an external verifier identity distinct from the runtime identity;
- emits the exact C17 control-plane receipt shape: OBSERVED_RUNTIME, exact source/runtime identity, authenticatedReadSucceeded=true, privateLifeStateExposed=false, writeAuthorityGranted=false, evidenceRef + independentVerifierRef;
- never grants write/deployment/business authority or infers provider independence.

Adds `scripts/founder-ops-runtime-probe.mjs`, an external authenticated GET probe. ADMIN_TOKEN is used only in the request header and is never serialized into the receipt/output.

Adds 8 hostile regressions for source drift, unauthorized/non-200 observation, private-vault leakage, network life-state authorization, authority inflation and runtime self-verification.

Execution boundary: current Vercel projects are still Hobby build-rate limited and GitHub Actions jobs are zero-step runner-allocation non-evidence, so this PR makes no observed hosted-control-plane claim. It creates the executable verifier needed for the next real named-host run; merge should wait for exact-head execution or equivalent focused execution evidence. No private founder data, provider call, deployment, spend or customer effect was performed.

Implements the missing C21 parent evidence tribunal over the already-merged C13 compound-intelligence evaluator instead of creating a second benchmark constitution.

Adds `src/system-level-asi-evidence.mjs` with the exact 20 canonical ASI capability dimensions from the Sovereign Cognitive Continuum north star. It only aggregates already-earned C13 evidence and is constitutionally unable to declare ASI.

Anti-cherry-picking rules:
- only the frozen canonical 20 dimensions may count;
- each counted dimension must carry fresh observed C13 `COMPOUND_INTELLIGENCE_GAIN_SUPPORTED_WITHIN_DEFINED_SCOPE` evidence bound to the exact candidate composition id/revision;
- C13 must already report fresh-context reproduced cross-domain transfer and keep `SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_NOT_ESTABLISHED`;
- baseline must have been verified at evaluation time, thresholds frozen before evaluation, fresh heldout retention explicit, contamination CLEAN or BOUNDED_DISCLOSED, and evaluator independence explicit;
- evidence refs and task-population hashes cannot be cloned across dimensions;
- critical dimensions (causal reasoning, planning under uncertainty, long-horizon coherence, transfer, self-improvement, adversarial robustness, calibrated refusal/ignorance) cannot be averaged away;
- at least three verifier identities and verifier lineages are required for partial/strong evidence staging;
- strong-within-defined-scope requires all 20 canonical dimensions; partial requires the configured breadth threshold plus every critical dimension; otherwise evidence stage remains not established.

Outputs are evidence stages only: `SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_EVIDENCE_NOT_ESTABLISHED`, `SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_EVIDENCE_PARTIAL`, or `SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_EVIDENCE_STRONG_WITHIN_DEFINED_SCOPE`. In every case `asiStatus` remains `SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_NOT_ESTABLISHED`, with promotion/self-modification/business-effect authority NONE.

Adds 12 hostile regressions for critical-dimension cherry-picking, cloned evidence, task-population reuse, stale evidence, wrong-candidate evidence, missing fresh retention, post-hoc thresholds, stale/unverified baseline selection, correlated verifier identities and ad-hoc denominator expansion.

Exact-head hosted execution is currently unavailable because both connected Vercel projects return Hobby build-rate-limit failures for this head. No hosted pass is claimed and this PR should remain unmerged until an executing exact-head or equivalent focused tribunal is available. No self-modification, deployment, provider call, spend, customer effect, AGI or ASI claim is created.

Closes a residual finite-denominator truth gap in the merged C11-B/C12 chain.

Observed defect on live main: C11-B required nonzero `counts.extractedConcepts` and exact materialized `counts.rows`, but did not require extractedConcepts == rows.length and only checked the declared byState counts summed to rows. The existing positive fixture itself demonstrated the hole: 12 extracted concepts with 10 materialized rows still certified exact-current truth. A same-total forged state histogram could likewise survive unless secondary semantic bindings happened to expose it.

This PR adds a shared denominator-conservation verifier used by both C12 graph compilation and C11-B receipt verification:
- every row state must be one of the canonical Sovereign coverage states;
- extractedConcepts == counts.rows == rows.length;
- byState must equal the exact histogram independently recomputed from materialized rows, not merely have the same total;
- C12 canonical binding now carries extractedConcepts and the observed row-derived state histogram;
- verifier-side canonical binding digest includes extractedConcepts, making the new denominator cryptographically load-bearing;
- C11-B independently requires graph coverageRows, extractedConcepts, state histogram and requirement count to agree with the regenerated coverage denominator.

Focused dependency-contract tribunal: 7/7 pass for valid conservation, extraction loss, same-total histogram forgery, unknown state injection, extracted-denominator binding drift, state-histogram binding drift and binding-digest mutation. Vercel remains Hobby build-rate-limited on the exact head and is infrastructure non-evidence, not a source failure.

No runtime, customer, payment, accepted-delivery, life-outcome, deployment or ASI evidence is created. Commercial truth remains external. Business-effect authority remains NONE and SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_NOT_ESTABLISHED remains explicit.

Closes a residual C11 evidence-chain gap after denominator conservation.

Before this PR, C11-B required readiness to report `measurementMode=LIVE_COMPUTED_FROM_IMPORT_GRAPH`, `partitionExact=true`, and `allClassified=true`, but trusted the emitted booleans. It did not independently prove that production + unattended-operator-only + founder-interactive-only + unreachable equals the declared reachability srcModules denominator, nor that readiness.repository.sourceModules equals that same denominator.

Adds `src/readiness-reachability-conservation.mjs` and composes it into C11-B:
- every reachability count must be an actual nonnegative safe integer;
- partition arithmetic is recomputed independently;
- `partitionExact` must agree with the arithmetic and must explicitly be true;
- readiness sourceModules must equal reachability srcModules;
- `allClassified=true` cannot contradict nonempty unclassified, stale-classification, or founder-interactive classification-violation lists;
- the positive C11 receipt uses the independently checked counts and marks the reachability denominator conserved.

Focused exact helper tribunal: 6/6 pass for valid partition, forged true partition flag with one missing module, false flag on balanced arithmetic, repository denominator drift, string-count coercion, and classification-list contradiction. Existing C11 explicit `reachability-partition-must-be-exact` refusal is preserved for compatibility.

Vercel remains Hobby build-rate-limited and is infrastructure non-evidence. No named-runtime, customer, payment, accepted-delivery, life-outcome, deployment, or ASI evidence is created. Business-effect authority remains NONE and SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_NOT_ESTABLISHED remains explicit.

Closes a residual C11-B/C12 evidence-chain gap on exact observed main `a59b9917b47e0731257d6bac028196637e2615b7` without changing unrelated swarm lanes.

The merged zero-orphan chain proves exact canonical requirement identity, finite denominator conservation, topology, semantic coverage content, reachability conservation and digest integrity. It did not yet independently prove that repository-backed evidence pointers named by coverage rows and generated leaves still resolve on the exact tracked tree. A graph could therefore remain structurally perfect while an internal source/test/artifact path had rotted underneath it.

Adds `src/evidence-reference-integrity.mjs`:
- exact `git ls-files` inventory is the repository existence authority;
- every declared internal source module must resolve and belong to a source-capable class (`src/`, `scripts/`, `api/`, `.claude/`);
- every declared test module must resolve under `tests/` and end in `.test.mjs`;
- repository-backed source artifacts and leaf exact-scope paths must resolve;
- non-boundary coverage rows require at least one repository-backed evidence reference;
- generated requirement `statusEvidenceRef` and leaf `inputEvidence` must remain bound to the exact canonical requirement id + current coverage state;
- external/owner/elapsed boundary rows are not forced to manufacture impossible repository evidence.

Adds `src/current-truth-reference-integrity.mjs` as a thin C11-B wrapper over the existing canonical verifier. Reference integrity is load-bearing before an otherwise-green truth receipt can pass; successful receipts carry a SHA-256 reference digest and retain commercial/runtime/life/ASI non-inference boundaries.

Updates `scripts/current-truth-regeneration.mjs` to read the exact tracked tree with `git ls-files` and feed it into the stronger verifier. No provider query, deployment, customer message, payment mutation, spend, private-life action or external effect is performed.

Focused isolated dependency-contract tribunal: 12/12 pass. It covers missing source refs, wrong-class test refs, internal rows with no repository evidence pointer, boundary exemption, status-evidence detachment, leaf-input detachment, missing exact-scope refs, load-bearing wrapper refusal, base-refusal preservation and reference-digest retention. This is focused source execution, not a whole-repo or named-host claim.

Vercel/GitHub capacity evidence remains infrastructure non-evidence unless an exact-head runner actually executes. Commercial truth remains external and `SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_NOT_ESTABLISHED` remains explicit.

Repairs the exact hosted C11/C12 failure observed on root Vercel branch `17a7112175b29542ab566b5bb4eab1239ef42a1e`.

Observed canonical coverage was internally consistent but intentionally canonicalized aliases: extractedConcepts=1068, rows=1038, mergedAliasRows=30. The newly merged denominator verifier incorrectly required extractedConcepts == materialized rows, contradicting the coverage compiler's longstanding no-drop law and its own tests, which define extractedConcepts == rows + mergedAliasRows.

This PR does not relax denominator conservation. It makes the real conservation equation explicit and load-bearing:
- `mergedAliasRows` must be an explicit nonnegative integer, never inferred from a convenient delta;
- declared rows must still equal materialized rows exactly;
- extractedConcepts must equal materialized rows + mergedAliasRows exactly;
- state histogram must still equal the materialized row-derived histogram exactly;
- denominator receipt exposes rows, extracted concepts, merged aliases and the conservation equation;
- hostile regressions cover valid one-alias collapse, omitted alias denominator, understated alias count and inflated alias count;
- current-truth fixtures now declare zero aliases explicitly rather than depending on an implicit assumption.

This is a truth-accounting correction only. It does not reduce the canonical extracted denominator, erase aliases, convert aliases into implementation work, or create runtime/customer/payment/life-outcome/ASI evidence. Business-effect authority remains NONE. The root Vercel project is the intended execution tribunal because it causally exposed the defect; merge requires clean exact-head execution or equivalent focused evidence.

Supersedes #555 on exact current main after adversarial review found that #555 validated a mutation-receipt shape the canonical Constraint Mutation engine did not emit. A hand-forged object could satisfy the old gate while a real canonical receipt could not.

This replacement composes the existing bounded-experiment, VOI and Constraint Mutation organs rather than creating a parallel framework.

Hardening:
- consumes the actual Constraint Mutation policy version/status/identity contract merged in #558;
- independently recomputes the canonical strategy fingerprint from objective/mechanism/provider/failure/signature fields;
- requires hardMutationRequired=true, identicalRetryAllowed=false and decision=MUTATE_STRATEGY_NOW;
- binds the mutation receipt to an explicit constraint objective;
- after a required mutation, the proposed mechanismId must differ from the failed canonical mechanismId;
- normalizes rival mechanism prose to reject punctuation/case/whitespace renames of the same mechanism;
- mechanism IDs must be unique when supplied;
- full bounded-experiment and VOI child outputs are SHA-256 bound into causal admission identity, so evidence/details cannot change behind a stable top-level status;
- optional unknown-unknown and mutation receipts are digest-bound too;
- output remains admission-only for the existing maintainer; C13/C26/recursive-governance gates still own later change/review/retention.

Focused hostile logic tribunal: 10/10 pass, covering real canonical-shaped mutation receipt, legacy forged receipt refusal, same failed mechanism formatting alias, wrong objective, fingerprint forgery, authority inflation, rival normalization, distinct mechanism, hidden VOI-detail digest drift, and bounded-probe digest drift.

A full checkout could not be executed in this session because container DNS cannot resolve github.com, while Vercel is Hobby build-rate-limited and GitHub jobs are zero-step infrastructure non-evidence. No hosted/full-suite claim is made. No write/promotion/self-modification/business-effect authority is created; SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_NOT_ESTABLISHED remains explicit.

Supersedes #554 after adversarial review found that its source-only CLI could read arbitrary JSON and directly emit `evidenceClass: OBSERVED_RUNTIME`. That let repository code manufacture the external runtime truth C17 is supposed to require. The old design also used raw case-sensitive identity comparisons, so provider/runtime/verifier aliases could fake independence.

This replacement keeps the useful C17 schemas and parent acceptance seam, but restores the truth boundary:

- source-only compilers create only `UNVERIFIED_RUNTIME_ASSERTION` with `originClass: SOURCE_ONLY_ASSERTION` and `maySatisfyRuntimeAcceptance: false`;
- a source-only CLI is explicitly named `runtime-transition-assertion` and states it does not observe a runtime or satisfy C17;
- `OBSERVED_RUNTIME` transition receipts are accepted only when bound to a separate executing-observer receipt with exact producer source commit, transition kind, subject assertion digest, runtime identity, observation time, independent verifier, zero duplicate effects, and no blind uncertain replay;
- observer and final receipt digests are independently recomputed;
- outer observed workload/cutover/provider semantics must exactly match the nested source assertion, preventing envelope laundering behind fresh digests;
- identity normalization uses Unicode NFKC, case folding, whitespace normalization, and repeated role-prefix stripping so `provider:Acme` vs ` ACME ` or `Verifier: Host-A` vs `runtime:host-a` cannot fake independence;
- cutover target must be the accepted host runtime;
- provider-loss alternate provider must actually own the accepted host, and failed/alternate provider identities must remain genuinely distinct;
- founder-private control-plane isolation remains required and write authority remains false;
- all source/output paths retain businessEffectAuthority NONE and ASI remains SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_NOT_ESTABLISHED.

Focused execution evidence in this run:
- runtime transition receipt/identity/observer logic tribunal: 17/17 pass;
- parent provider-neutral runtime acceptance composition against the current PostgreSQL restore receipt contract: 9/9 pass.
These are focused dependency-contract executions, not a whole-repo, named-host, cutover, provider-loss or elapsed-autonomy claim.

Crucially, this PR does NOT claim an executing observer currently exists or that any provider-loss/cutover event happened. It makes those real-world receipts impossible for the source-only compiler to mint and leaves actual runtime observation as an external/runtime evidence requirement.

Follow-up hardening after merged #562. Independent diff review found that #562's executing-observer receipt was still source-constructible JSON protected only by recomputable SHA-256 digests. A caller that can construct that object can also recompute those digests, so the parent C17 acceptance gate still needed a trust root outside repository-controlled input.

This PR adds a narrow external attestation boundary instead of replacing #562:
- `src/runtime-evidence-attestation.mjs` defines a canonical bundle over exact source commit, accepted host runtime/provider, and the exact durable-workload/cutover/provider-loss receipt digests;
- `verifyProviderNeutralRuntimeAcceptance()` now requires an Ed25519 signature over that bundle;
- the verification public key comes only from protected runtime configuration `UBERBOND_RUNTIME_EVIDENCE_PUBLIC_KEY_PEM`, never from the receipt/input;
- the attestation binds the configured public-key fingerprint, so an attacker cannot substitute a self-generated signing key;
- missing key, missing signature, attacker-key substitution, post-signature transition-digest mutation, or host/provider drift fails closed;
- source-only assertions, existing semantic/digest integrity checks, private founder-life isolation, zero business-effect authority, and `SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_NOT_ESTABLISHED` remain unchanged.

Focused dependency-contract execution of the exact new attestation module: 6/6 pass with a real ephemeral Ed25519 keypair. Cases: trusted signature positive path; missing attestation; missing configured trust root; attacker-generated replacement key; transition receipt digest mutation; host/provider mutation. Syntax check passed for the attestation module. This is scoped evidence for the new cryptographic delta, not whole-repo or named-runtime proof.

GitHub exact-head jobs allocated but returned `steps:null`, which is runner-allocation infrastructure non-evidence. Local full checkout is also blocked by DNS resolution of github.com. Those failures are not counted as source failures.

No private key is committed or requested. No runtime, provider-loss, cutover, customer, payment, deployment, spend, life-outcome or ASI event is claimed.

Follow-up to merged #563 after adversarial review found its initial Ed25519 attestation covered only source commit, runtime/provider identity, and the three transition receipt digests. That left other acceptance-critical runtime witnesses mutable after signing.

This PR is intentionally narrow: exact current main plus only two changed files.

Hardening:
- runtime attestation payload now binds the accepted host's runtime identity, provider, region, image digest, config digest, data-schema digest, source commit and authenticated-health observation;
- it cryptographically hashes the full stable objects for all seven acceptance-critical witnesses: PostgreSQL restore, restart recovery, durable workload, cutover/rollback, continuity rehearsal, provider loss, and founder control-plane observation;
- full-object hashing means a caller cannot mutate a child receipt while retaining an old self-declared `receiptDigest` and still satisfy the signature;
- protected trust root must parse specifically as Ed25519; RSA or attacker-substituted keys fail closed;
- public-key fingerprint remains bound to the protected configured key, not caller input;
- canonical evidence hashing is bounded to depth 64, 10,000 object nodes and 1 MiB serialized canonical form; cyclic, over-deep, over-large or otherwise noncanonical evidence produces no digest and fails closed rather than crashing verification.

Focused evidence earned in this run:
- trust-root/crypto hostile tribunal: 11/11 pass;
- parent provider-neutral runtime acceptance integration with correctly signed full bundle: 12/12 pass, including missing signature and post-signature PostgreSQL/control-plane mutation refusal.
These are focused dependency-contract executions, not a whole-repo or named-runtime claim.

No private signing key is committed or requested. No runtime event, cutover, provider loss, customer, payment, deployment, spend, life outcome, AGI or ASI fact is created by this code. The actual signer and real observations remain external/runtime evidence requirements.

Adversarial follow-up to merged C17 trust-anchor work on exact current main `0e55b9096ffddd03db48746e59a237f1f5402a6c`.

Found a concrete cryptographic-completeness defect in the v1.1 full-object attestation: its canonicalizer ultimately relied on JavaScript `JSON.stringify` coercion. Two post-signature object mutations can therefore preserve the exact signed digest: adding an `undefined` property is omitted from object JSON, and changing a legitimate `null` field to `NaN` serializes back to `null`. Functions/symbols can also disappear, while exotic object prototypes/accessors are not a safe evidence language.

This PR upgrades only the existing C17 attestation owner rather than adding another trust framework:
- runtime evidence attestation contract v1.2;
- canonical evidence values are restricted to strict inert JSON data: null, strings, booleans, finite non-negative-zero numbers, arrays, and plain/null-prototype objects;
- undefined, functions, symbols, bigint, NaN/Infinity, negative zero, exotic prototypes and accessor properties fail closed;
- existing depth/node/1MiB bounds remain;
- unsupported/cyclic/oversized evidence yields no digest, so it cannot satisfy the Ed25519 acceptance gate;
- trust-root semantics, host/evidence binding, private founder-life isolation, zero business-effect authority, and SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_NOT_ESTABLISHED remain unchanged.

Focused isolated execution of the exact updated self-contained module: syntax clean; 6/6 targeted tribunal passes, including valid Ed25519 positive path, previously invisible undefined mutation, null→NaN JSON collision, executable/exotic values, cycle refusal and depth refusal. Repository search found no duplicated hard-coded v1.1 consumer outside the owner module; consumers/tests import the exported version.

No runtime event, provider call, deployment, spend, customer/payment state, life outcome, signing private key or ASI fact is created. Hosted full-repo execution remains subject to current external runner/Vercel capacity.

Closes a residual C11-B/C12 evidence-chain weakness on exact observed main `0e55b9096ffddd03db48746e59a237f1f5402a6c` without touching unrelated swarm lanes.

The existing evidence-reference verifier correctly checked row, requirement, leaf, scope and coverage-state relationships, but its durable `referenceDigest` committed only to coverage source commit, requirement IDs, the union of checked repository paths, and tracked-path count. Reassigning the same valid repository path set between canonical rows/leaves could therefore leave the reference receipt digest unchanged even though the evidence assignment changed. Parent coverage/graph digests catch many such mutations today, but the reference receipt itself was weaker than its semantic claim.

This PR makes the reference proof independently tamper-evident:
- bumps the evidence reference verifier to v1.1;
- canonicalizes and binds per-row current state + source/test/artifact references;
- binds per-requirement canonical source, exact status evidence and execution leaf IDs;
- binds per-leaf requirement ownership, exact scope and input evidence;
- preserves deterministic digest stability under harmless array/input ordering;
- exposes binding counts in the receipt;
- keeps the current-truth wrapper schema stable while separately recording the exact underlying verifier version, so future verifier upgrades cannot masquerade as the old proof generation.

Focused isolated execution of the semantic-digest delta: 3/3 pass, including same-path-set reassignment changing the digest and harmless ordering preserving it. Repository tests add hostile regressions for those properties plus wrapper-version provenance. This is focused source evidence, not whole-repo or named-runtime proof.

No runtime, customer, payment, accepted-delivery, retention, life-outcome, deployment, spend or ASI fact is created. Commercial truth remains external, businessEffectAuthority remains NONE, and SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_NOT_ESTABLISHED remains intact.

Closes two finite C17 runtime-evidence integrity gaps on exact observed main `43f0c3ebd6b3e2176b42482f15a62fec2d2fea73` without creating another runtime framework.

1. Founder/iPad control-plane witness hardening:
- bumps founder-ops runtime probe to v1.2;
- exports exact receipt preimage + independent integrity verifier;
- verifies schema/status/class, exact source SHA, canonical HTTPS target/target identity, runtime identity, observed-view digest, read-only/private-life invariants, evidence/verifier refs, timestamp and recomputed digest;
- reuses normalized C17 identity equivalence so casing/whitespace/role-prefix aliases cannot fake verifier independence;
- parent named-runtime acceptance makes canonical control-plane receipt integrity load-bearing.

2. Restart/recovery witness hardening:
- bumps restart receipt to v1.1;
- replaces arbitrary text source identity with mandatory exact 40-hex source commit;
- adds canonical receipt preimage, SHA-256 digest and independent integrity verifier;
- integrity covers observed crash/recovery/replacement/dead-letter/cleanup facts, executed commands, duplicate-effect claim, rollback boundary and zero business authority;
- parent named-runtime acceptance now requires canonical restart receipt integrity and exact source binding rather than trusting a few loose fields.

Tests update the positive named-runtime fixture to compose canonical producer outputs and add hostile regressions for post-observation control-plane mutation, forged control schema/status/digest/target identity, verifier aliases, malformed/short restart source identity, restart digest mutation and observed restart-state mutation.

This PR does not claim that any control-plane request, independent host, restart, restore, cutover, provider loss or elapsed-autonomy event actually occurred. It only hardens the source contracts that judge such evidence. Business-effect authority remains NONE and SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_NOT_ESTABLISHED remains unchanged.

Closes a concrete C21 evaluator-independence seam on exact observed main `43f0c3ebd6b3e2176b42482f15a62fec2d2fea73` without adding another evaluation constitution.

The existing system-level ASI evidence tribunal correctly required multiple verifier identities/lineages, but counted caller-supplied verifier strings literally. Cosmetic aliases such as role prefixes, case changes and whitespace could therefore inflate apparent verifier diversity even when the same evaluator lineage supplied the evidence.

This PR hardens the existing `src/system-level-asi-evidence.mjs` parent:
- bumps C21 evidence protocol to v1.2;
- applies the repository's already-established C17-style semantic identity rule at the C21 evaluator boundary: Unicode NFKC, case folding, whitespace normalization and repeated role-prefix stripping;
- counts normalized verifier identities and normalized lineages, not raw caller spelling;
- normalizes evaluator evidence references and refuses one evaluator record cloned across dimensions under cosmetic relabeling;
- preserves authenticated exact-candidate C13 receipt binding, fresh-context retention, matched-budget transfer evidence, contamination disclosure, critical-dimension requirements, frozen thresholds, strongest-baseline verification and canonical 20-dimension denominator;
- preserves `SYSTEM_LEVEL_ASI_NOT_ESTABLISHED`, `promotionAuthority: NONE`, `selfModificationAuthority: NONE` and `businessEffectAuthority: NONE`.

Adds hostile regressions proving `Verifier: Eval-A`, ` eval-a `, `EVALUATOR: EVAL-A`, and `reviewer: eval-a` collapse to one verifier identity, lineage casing/whitespace aliases collapse to one lineage, and a cosmetically relabeled evaluator record cannot be counted twice.

Execution boundary: both connected Vercel projects currently report the Hobby build-rate limit, GitHub has no workflow run for the exact head, and the independent local checkout attempt failed because the execution container cannot resolve `github.com`. Those are infrastructure non-evidence, so this PR is intentionally left unmerged pending executing exact-head/focused evidence. No ASI, deployment, self-modification, provider, customer, payment or external-effect claim is created.

Repairs the exact root-Vercel C11/C12 truth-regeneration failure observed after current readiness/coverage successfully regenerated on the #567 build.

Observed hosted evidence at `a6d4f54d332fc25a6322592c95a0dfc352c8a4c7`:
- readiness generated 33 capabilities;
- Sovereign coverage compiled 1,068 extracted concepts into 1,038 canonical rows + 30 merged aliases;
- canonical execution graph materialized 1,121 leaves with 0 orphans and 0 floating leaves;
- reference integrity then correctly refused `total-brain:frontier-engine` because `tests/helpers/frontier-synthetic-provenance.mjs` appeared in `currentEvidence.testModules` even though test-module evidence is required to be `tests/**/*.test.mjs`.

Root cause: `scripts/sovereign-coverage-matrix.mjs` indexed every `.mjs` recursively under `tests/` as executable test evidence. That includes helpers imported by tests. The downstream verifier was stricter and correct.

Fix:
- coverage repoIndex now exposes only `*.test.mjs` paths as `testFiles`;
- helper/support modules remain tracked repository files but cannot inflate implementation proof by masquerading as executed tests;
- exports repoIndex for direct contract testing;
- regression proves the test evidence class contains only `tests/**/*.test.mjs` and specifically excludes `tests/helpers/frontier-synthetic-provenance.mjs`.

This does not lower the evidence bar, change the canonical denominator, erase concepts, create runtime/customer/payment/life/ASI proof, or create business-effect authority. The intended tribunal is the root Vercel build that causally exposed the wrong-class reference.

Adversarial current-main audit found a stale tracked `lite/public/uberbond.js` that still read `revenueEngineToken` / `nightshiftToken` from localStorage and wrote the submitted owner token back to localStorage. The canonical root Command Center client has already moved owner authority to page memory only.

The lite build already overwrites this stale file from canonical `public/uberbond.js` before deployment, so this PR does not claim a presently deployed Vercel leak. It closes the remaining source/local-static drift seam instead of inventing a second auth implementation:

- deletes the divergent tracked `lite/public/uberbond.js`;
- keeps the existing `lite/scripts/build-visual-cortex.mjs` copy-from-canonical architecture;
- adds `tests/lite-owner-bearer-source.test.mjs`, which fails if the canonical client regresses to persistent privileged storage, if a second tracked lite owner client returns, or if the lite build stops explicitly regenerating `uberbond.js` from the canonical source;
- wires that regression into the existing lite build tribunal.

No credential value is read, migrated, printed or changed. No provider call, deployment authority, customer action, payment action, private-life access or business-effect authority is created. Hosted execution is required for a deployment claim; source review alone proves only the removal of the stale duplicate and the new regression contract.

Clean current-main successor to historical PR #430. The old branch contains unrelated drift; this PR transplants only the two causal files onto exact current main `e3938639c9f568de8c62cea806d4b388eeece3ca`.

Problem preserved from real Vercel evidence: when the build runs as root, `embedded-postgres` can spawn `initdb` under the `postgres` uid/gid. Current main only probes PostgreSQL binaries as the parent process, so it can report READY while the actual child identity later hits EACCES.

Changes:
- resolve the same `postgres` uid/gid on root Linux builds when available;
- probe `initdb`, `pg_ctl`, and `postgres` under that child identity;
- restore directory search permission and fixture readability needed by that child inside the ephemeral build tree;
- preserve the pinned `@embedded-postgres/linux-x64@18.4.0-beta.17` contract and bounded temp mirror fallback;
- extend the existing fixture regression with child-identity wiring and a locked-path traversal test.

Independent local Linux tribunal on the exact transplanted mechanism: 3/3 pass (child-identity wiring, default fixture execution, locked-path search restoration). Historical #430 evidence remains donor evidence only, including its earlier Mutation War and Whole Brain results.

Merge hold remains platform-specific: the root Vercel project must execute this current branch and cross the historical `initdb EACCES` boundary under its real `postgres` child identity. A Vercel quota refusal is infrastructure non-evidence. No customer/payment/outbound/credential/spend/private-life/model authority is broadened.

Implements the cache-economics half of donor issue #574 as a thin extension of the existing `src/vercel-ai-gateway-executor.mjs`, not a new router or cache framework.

Current official Vercel AI Gateway documentation now explicitly supports `providerOptions.gateway.caching = 'auto'` on OpenAI Chat Completions, which is UberBond's existing transport. This PR uses that exact current surface only when a caller explicitly supplies stable shared context.

Safety/economic semantics:
- shared cache context must be a string, bounded to 200 KB, and carry an explicit approved data class: PUBLIC, INTERNAL_NON_SECRET, or SOURCE_CODE;
- unlabeled context and founder-private classes fail before any provider call;
- stable shared context is placed before request-specific task material for exact-prefix reuse;
- raw shared context is never copied into result receipts; only byte count + SHA-256 are retained;
- cache reads/writes are evidence only when provider usage fields are actually present and valid;
- impossible cache counters fail closed;
- cache savings are never computed without separately verified cache pricing;
- pre-call reservation and post-call cost remain at the existing full uncached input/output rates, preserving the existing `CONFIGURED_CONSERVATIVE_ESTIMATE` accounting contract;
